From 30172d2a39fa19fa093d1ec71d40ca8d84eaa066 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harry Wentland <harry.wentland@amd.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 11:53:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: add RGBA8888 surface pixel format support

amdgpu_dm advertises DRM_FORMAT_RGBA8888 for its planes, but the DC
surface_pixel_format enum only had the ARGB8888 and ABGR8888 variants.
fill_dc_plane_info_and_addr() therefore fell through to the default
case and rejected RGBA8888 with -EINVAL, even though the hardware
supports it: the HUBP/DPP SURFACE_PIXEL_FORMAT field has a dedicated
RGBA8888 encoding (value 9) next to ARGB8888 (value 8).

Add SURFACE_PIXEL_FORMAT_GRPH_RGBA8888 and plumb it through:

 - map DRM_FORMAT_RGBA8888 to the new format in the DM;
 - program the dedicated register value 9 in the HUBP and DPP across
   all DCN generations (no red/blue crossbar swap, unlike ABGR);
 - treat it as a 32bpp graphics format everywhere else (bandwidth,
   bytes-per-pixel, DCC and format-class helpers), identical to
   ARGB8888.

Closes: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/drm/amd/-/work_items/5339
Assisted-by: Copilot:claude-opus-4.8
Signed-off-by: Harry Wentland <harry.wentland@amd.com>
